WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.110
I made Duckling Tablet for my daughter, Scarlett.

2
00:00:04.183 --> 00:00:12.623
On a tablet that is not locked down, there are ads everywhere, and one video leads to the next until a child ends up somewhere inappropriate.

3
00:00:13.917 --> 00:00:19.397
On a Duckling tablet, kids can open only the learning apps and the websites their parents allow.

4
00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:26.177
Every app is designed to move a child forward a little at a time, starting at their own level.

5
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:31.730
As they learn and play, they earn stars to decorate their own avatar.

6
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:39.890
When I saw her progress in reading and math, I decided to share it with other families. Here is how to set it up.

7
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.510
Go to parents.ducklingtablet.com, and type your email.

8
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:49.937
Open the link in the email. Your first sign in creates the family.

9
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.697
Add your child with a first name and an age.

10
00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.510
Each subject starts at a level that fits their age.

11
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:04.443
Open the app store on the tablet and search for Duckling Tablet: Kids Learning.

12
00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:09.297
On the website, choose your child and make a pairing code.

13
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:14.403
Type the code on the tablet, give it a name, and press Pair.

14
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.363
Choose a four-digit parent PIN, and type it twice.

15
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:26.550
The parent area lists the steps that lock the tablet down. When every step is finished, press Done.

16
00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:31.183
The tablet is ready, with the starter apps installed.

17
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.250
On the website, the tablet now shows under Devices.

18
00:01:37.717 --> 00:01:40.997
Under Parents, invite the other parent by email.

19
00:01:42.017 --> 00:01:45.137
They get an email with a link that works for seven days.

20
00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:49.443
The link signs them in to the same family.

21
00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.270
Each new tablet gets its own pairing code.

22
00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.110
The new tablet has the same apps, levels, and stars for Scarlett.

23
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:06.703
Both tablets are listed under Devices, and any parent can manage them.

24
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:12.303
On your phone, the website can sit on your home screen, and it opens like an app.

25
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:21.543
On an iPhone, the home screen app keeps its own sign-in, so the email has a six-digit code to type in. On Android, the link in the email works.

26
00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.190
After that, it opens straight to your family.

27
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:31.030
Search the apps for what your child wants. When nothing fits, press Ask for this app.

28
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:36.443
Describe the app and what your child likes about it, then send the request.

29
00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:42.683
The request is listed with its status, and requests are included with the subscription.

30
00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:49.383
Under Websites, type the address of a site, give its tile a name, and press Allow site.

31
00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:55.523
Every tablet in the family gets the tile, and sites that are not allowed stay blocked.

32
00:02:56.617 --> 00:03:03.377
Under Other apps, the website lists the apps on an Android tablet. Press Allow to put one on its home screen.

33
00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:11.637
You decide how many minutes a day it gets and the hours it can open, and when the time ends, the tablet comes back to Duckling.

34
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:15.977
The tablet shows the app with the time it has left today.

35
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:22.910
On an iPad, the apps are chosen on the iPad itself, in the parent area under Other apps.

36
00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:27.663
Set up your family at parents.ducklingtablet.com.
